00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.000
Yeah, I'd even say that it goes even further.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.780
Like, the actual, like, yes, it's a side-scroller.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.620
But it also just, like, really feels like Zelda 2.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.360
Down to just, like, the moment-to-moment.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.040
Like, oh, that jump feels like the jump from Zelda 2.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:41.080
That kind of stuff. Yeah, it's that, like, platform-y combat side-scrolling that, like, that Zelda 2 sort of made popular, I guess.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:47.800
You know, or Faxanadu being the other example that we recently played.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:58.620
Yeah, and I think with Faxanadu, the difference was the exploration of the map was all, you were always on the same map.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.420
